Researchers developing high-assurance software need a platform-independent graphical interface for the High Assurance Transformation System. Users should be able to prepare transformation applications, invoke proven transformations on abstract programs, and inspect or manipulate the resulting output without working directly with the underlying command-oriented services. The interface should make experimentation with semantics-preserving program transformation more accessible while retaining confidence in the transformed results.

Current Slots:
[
  {
    "name": "project_goals",
    "category": "goals",
    "value": "Let researchers work with the transformation system without having to use the command line or low-level service calls; make it faster to set up a transformation, run proven transformations on abstract programs, and inspect results clearly enough to support experimentation and iteration; reduce setup friction while preserving confidence that outputs remain semantically sound."
  },
  {
    "name": "stakeholder_roles",
    "category": "stakeholders",
    "value": "Primary users are researchers working on high-assurance software transformations, able to create transformation requests, run approved transformations, and inspect outputs. Some users may have read-only access to review results, while others need full access to prepare and execute experiments. Administrators or technical maintainers manage platform setup, transformation definitions, and possibly access control. Reviewers or collaborators can inspect logs or outputs without changing transformation inputs."
  },
  {
    "name": "functional_needs",
    "category": "functionality",
    "value": "Provide a graphical interface for importing or selecting abstract programs, preparing transformation applications, choosing proven transformations, configuring required parameters, invoking transformations, and inspecting or manipulating the resulting output. Support creation of transformation requests, execution of approved transformations, and viewing of results, intermediate artifacts, and logs with possible read-only and full-access modes."
  },
  {
    "name": "business_rules",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": "A transformation may be executed only if the input program and transformation configuration are complete and valid, and the transformation is one of the proven, approved transformations available in the system. The interface must prevent launching transformations that are missing required parameters or have not passed required validation. Regular researchers may prepare and execute permitted transformations, while changes to approved transformations or system-level settings are restricted to maintainers or admins. If edits would invalidate an approved transformation request, the GUI should block them unless the user explicitly revalidates the request."
  },
  {
    "name": "data_entities",
    "category": "data",
    "value": "Abstract program, transformation request/application, proven transformation, transformation configuration, transformation metadata, configuration file, generated output, intermediate artifacts, logs."
  },
  {
    "name": "constraints",
    "category": "constraints",
    "value": "Platform-independent graphical interface; should avoid requiring direct use of command-oriented services; transformations must remain proven/semantics-preserving to retain trust in results; some users may have read-only access while others have full access depending on environment and role."
  },
  {
    "name": "quality_concerns",
    "category": "quality",
    "value": "Usability, accessibility, reduced setup time, clarity of result inspection, support for experimentation and iteration, early surfacing of validation errors or unsupported input formats, and confidence/trust in semantic correctness of outputs."
  },
  {
    "name": "boundary_conditions",
    "category": "exceptions",
    "value": "Unsupported input formats and validation errors should be surfaced early before execution rather than allowing the run to fail later. The GUI should handle cases where edits would invalidate an approved transformation request by blocking the change until revalidation occurs."
  },
