    "value": "Prepared, approved, runnable/executable, executed, and requiring revalidation if edited in a way that invalidates an approved request."
  },
  {
    "name": "audit_and_provenance_requirements",
    "category": "quality",
    "value": "The GUI should present transformation metadata, configuration files, generated output, intermediate artifacts, and logs so researchers can understand and reproduce runs; full audit/provenance requirements are not yet defined."
  },
  {
    "name": "error_handling_and_validation_rules",
    "category": "exceptions",
    "value": "Reject or block transformation execution when the input program or transformation configuration is incomplete or invalid, or when required parameters are missing. Prevent use of transformations that have not been proven or approved. Surface unsupported input formats and validation errors early before execution. Block edits that would invalidate an approved transformation request unless the user explicitly revalidates it."
  },
